<div class="component container col-12">
    <div class="component-content" >

    <div class="component footnotes col-12">
        <div class="component-content">
<div class="cf-footnotes">
    <h5>Footnotes</h5>
        <ol>
                    <li id="cf-fn-1">Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland (2005).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-1" aria-label="Return from footnote 1.">Return to 1</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-2">Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland (2006).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-2" aria-label="Return from footnote 2.">Return to 2</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-3">Lin (2012).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-3" aria-label="Return from footnote 3.">Return to 3</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-4">See Mester (2017) and Braunstein (2008).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-4" aria-label="Return from footnote 4.">Return to 4</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-5">The Federal Reserve, the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC), and the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency (OCC) are currently working together to strengthen and modernize the regulations that implement the CRA. See Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (September 21, 2020) and Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, Office of the Comptroller of the Currency (July 20, 2021).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-5" aria-label="Return from footnote 5.">Return to 5</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-6">Kodrzycki and Mu&ntilde;oz, et al. (2009).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-6" aria-label="Return from footnote 6.">Return to 6</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-7">These sectors were health care in western Pennsylvania, information technology (IT) in northeastern Ohio, advanced manufacturing in central Ohio, marine mechanics in northwestern Ohio, and coal mining in eastern Kentucky. Four of these five initiatives provide direct training to workers, while the IT initiative focuses on increasing and enhancing the pipeline of IT talent through deep employer engagement with educational institutions at all levels. See Fee, Klesta, and Nelson (2016).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-7" aria-label="Return from footnote 7.">Return to 7</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-8">In the survey, which was conducted in December 2021 and January 2022, 78 percent of respondents said they were struggling to find talent, citing recruitment as their biggest challenge, and 94 percent of respondents said that their pool of qualified applicants was insufficient to meet their needs. See Burke (2022).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-8" aria-label="Return from footnote 8.">Return to 8</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-9">See Burke (2022).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-9" aria-label="Return from footnote 9.">Return to 9</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-10">See Nelson and Goran (2022) for further discussion.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-10" aria-label="Return from footnote 10.">Return to 10</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-11">For more information on benefits cliffs and CLIFF, see the Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta, Advancing Careers for Low-Income Families.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-11" aria-label="Return from footnote 11.">Return to 11</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-12">See Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland (2021).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-12" aria-label="Return from footnote 12.">Return to 12</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-13">See Mester (2021).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-13" aria-label="Return from footnote 13.">Return to 13</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-14">The Federal Reserve System worked with the John J. Heldrich Center for Workforce Development at Rutgers University, the Ray Marshall Center of the Lyndon B. Johnson School at the University of Texas, and the W.E. Upjohn Institute for Employment Research on the initiative, Investing in America&rsquo;s Workforce.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-14" aria-label="Return from footnote 14.">Return to 14</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-15">Pack and Fee (2019).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-15" aria-label="Return from footnote 15.">Return to 15</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-16">Fee (2020, 2021), Pacetti (2018), and Barkley, Pacetti, and Bailey (2018).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-16" aria-label="Return from footnote 16.">Return to 16</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-17">Wardrip, et al. (2015).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-17" aria-label="Return from footnote 17.">Return to 17</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-18">The tool is available at the Occupational Mobility Explorer web page.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-18" aria-label="Return from footnote 18.">Return to 18</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-19">See Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland (2020) and Nelson, Fee, and Wardrip (2019).
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-19" aria-label="Return from footnote 19.">Return to 19</a>
                    </li>
        </ol>
</div>
        </div>
    </div>
